course: dictionary
lesson: 11048
title: Words for a family celebration
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wedding is a ceremony and celebration where two people get married. Read the words around it for clues. «In Bradford, Hamid goes to a wedding with 300 guests» tells you a wedding can be a very big event, and «gets his cheeks pinched by about 20 aunties» tells you his family is there too.
explain: Weddings look different in different places and faiths. They can happen in churches, mosques, synagogues, temples, gurdwaras, register offices or outdoors. Customs vary, but many have rings, vows, a cake, speeches and dancing. Always ask: would a word like "party" fit? It might, but a wedding is a special celebration where two people get married.
explain: «Picture a wedding in a hotel near Galway: your cousin is a bridesmaid in a matching dress.» A bridesmaid helps the bride on the wedding day, and the matching dress is another clue. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A wedding is a ceremony and celebration where two people get married.
fact: A wedding anniversary is the same date every year after a couple married.
fact: Weddings can take place in churches, mosques, synagogues, temples, gurdwaras, register offices or outdoors.
fact: Common wedding words include bride, groom, ring, vows, cake and speeches.
fact: Cousins are the children of your aunts and uncles, and some cousins only meet at weddings and funerals.
exercise: «In Bradford, Hamid goes to a wedding with 300 guests.» What is a wedding? | *A ceremony and celebration where two people get married | A race around the park | A shop that sells birthday cards | A school trip to the seaside
exercise: «Your cousin is a bridesmaid in a matching dress.» What does bridesmaid suggest? | A grandma who cooks the food | *Someone who helps the bride on her wedding day | A driver who takes guests home | A dog wearing a bow tie
exercise: «Some cousins only meet at weddings and funerals.» What are cousins? | The guests who sing at weddings | The people who make the wedding cake | *The children of your aunts and uncles | Your teachers at school
test: What does «wedding anniversary» mean? | *The same date every year after a couple married | A church bell that rings for a long time | A cake shaped like a heart | The day a baby is born
test: In «Picture a wedding in a hotel near Galway», where is the wedding? | *A hotel near Galway | A school in Dublin | A zoo | A mountain
exam: Hamid goes to a wedding with 300 guests. What does this tell you about weddings? | They only happen in schools | They are the same as funerals | They are always quiet and private | *They can be very big celebrations with many people
